      "id": 1,
      "text": "Bristow’s main road, Linton Hall Road, was named after the 1922-founded Linton Hall Military School.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bristow%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Battle of Bristoe Station and the Battle of Kettle Run were fought on Bristow’s historic “hallowed ground” in 1862 and 1863.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpwc.com/plan-your-trip/neighborhoods/bristow/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bristow hosts the Bristoe Station Battlefield Heritage Park, a 140‑acre Civil War site perfect for family hikes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpwc.com/plan-your-trip/neighborhoods/bristow/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Brentsville Historic District, including the 1822 courthouse and a one‑room schoolhouse, sits within Bristow’s borders.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitpwc.com/plan-your-trip/neighborhoods/bristow/"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Linton family’s former plantation land, once owned by the 18th‑century Lintons, now contains the Braemar Community and its cemetery.",
